  "answer_text": "Here is an overview of **ProFed Credit Union** (profedcu.org):\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfe6 About ProFed Credit Union\n\nFounded in 1933, ProFed Credit Union is a **$740 million financial cooperative** with nearly **66,000 member-owners**. It provides financial services to members and businesses all over **northeast Indiana**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf10 Website\nThe official website is **[www.profedcu.org](https://www.profedcu.org)** *(note: profedcreditunion.com redirects or is associated with this main site).*\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udc65 Membership\n\n- You can own a piece of the credit union with just **$5**. Membership gets you exclusive access to **lower fees and competitive rates**, plus local, personalized service, discounted perks, and a cooperative that supports your community.\n- You are eligible to join if you **live, work, worship, attend school, volunteer, or regularly conduct business** in Adams, Allen, DeKalb, Huntington, LaGrange, Noble, Steuben, Wells, and Whitley counties.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccd Branches & Locations\n\n- ProFed has **13 branch locations** in northeast Indiana.\n- Branches are located in communities including **Fort Wayne, Auburn, Decatur, New Haven, Bluffton, Angola, and Columbia City**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcda Financial Resources\n\n- ProFed offers a wide range of resources for kids, adults, and businesses \u2014 from **budgeting basics to investing and planning for retirement** \u2014 and it's free to the community.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcbc For Employees\n\n- Full-time employees receive a **comprehensive benefits package**, including tuition reimbursement, vacation and personal time, and paid holidays. Part-time benefits are also offered.\n\n---\n\nIs there something specific about ProFed Credit Union you'd like to know more about, such as their loan products, membership process, or branch locations?",
